Ladybird now gives a table laid out in fixed mode with a percentage
width a max-content inline size of 1,000,000px. That matches WebKit,
whose FixedTableLayout::applyContentLogicalWidthQuirks() raises such a
table’s max width to tableMaxWidth (1000000), and Blink, whose
TableLayoutAlgorithm::ComputeMinMaxSizes() sets its max size to
TableTypes::kTableMaxInlineSize (also 1000000). Gecko goes further: Its
FixedTableLayoutStrategy::GetPrefISize() returns nscoord_MAX for every
fixed-layout table. The exact value is copied from WebKit and Blink, as
it decides the width of any shrink-to-fit container wider than that.
